---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import RoomSketch from "../components/RoomSketch.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

const matchCode = `import { beginMatch } from "@parlor/convex";

// Inside your authenticated game mutation:
const match = await beginMatch(ctx, {
  roomId,
  actor,
  minPlayers: 3,
  maxPlayers: 12,
});

// The lineup is frozen. The game is yours.
await startYourGame(ctx, match.id);`;
const packages = [
  { name: "core", text: "The rules beneath the rules.", description: "Room codes, player bounds, presence, and domain types." },
  { name: "auth", text: "A seat, not a sign-up.", description: "Signed guest credentials, with server-side verification." },
  { name: "convex", text: "Everyone on the same page.", description: "Rooms, membership, host transfer, and match lifecycles." },
  { name: "react", text: "Ready for the small screen.", description: "Room inputs, QR codes, connection state, and presence hooks." },
  { name: "web", text: "The little things that matter.", description: "Wake locks, credential storage, and game-night audio cues." },
];
---
<Base>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="intro-pill"><span></span>Open-source multiplayer for game night</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Make room<br />for play.</h1>
        <p class="hero-description">You bring the game. We’ll bring everyone together.</p>
        <p class="hero-detail">Rooms, guest identity, presence, and match lifecycles for Convex and React. All the shared plumbing. None of your game rules.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Start building</a><a class="button button-outline" href="/docs/agents/">Give your agent the docs</a></div>
        <p class="hero-footnote">TypeScript throughout. MIT licensed. Built for real friends.</p>
      </div>
      <RoomSketch />
    </section>

    <div class="proof-strip"><div class="container proof-inner"><p>Less setup between “want to play?” and playing.</p><a href="https://poppycock.mistystep.io">Already bringing people together in <strong>Poppycock <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></strong></a></div></div>

    <section id="why-parlor" class="section container why-section" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="why-title">Build the fun part.</h2><p>Every party game needs a room.<br />Not every party game should have to build one.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-visual code-visual" aria-hidden="true"><span>P</span><span>L</span><span>A</span><span>Y</span></div>
        <div><h3>From “join us” to all of us.</h3><p>Share a short room code or a QR link. Players join as guests, from the phone already in their pocket. No accounts standing between friends and the first round.</p></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/rooms-and-presence/">Meet the room</a>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-visual presence-visual" aria-hidden="true"><span>A</span><span>J</span><span>S</span><i></i></div>
        <div><h3>Phones sleep. Life happens.</h3><p>Visibility-aware heartbeats keep presence honest. If the host leaves, another active player takes over. You decide how your game handles an interruption.</p></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/rooms-and-presence/#heartbeats-and-host-self-healing">Follow the lifecycle</a>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-visual match-visual" aria-hidden="true"><span>Round<br /><strong>2</strong></span><i>+1</i></div>
        <div><h3>There’s always room for a rematch.</h3><p>Each match gets its own frozen lineup. Late arrivals don’t change a game in progress; they can play in the next one. Same room. New possibilities.</p></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/matches/">Understand matches</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ownership-section" aria-labelledby="ownership-title"><div class="container ownership-grid">
      <div class="ownership-copy"><h2 id="ownership-title">Your rules.<br />Our room.</h2><p>Parlor is a toolkit, not a game engine. Keep your prompts, scoring, phases, and visual personality. Let the shared foundation stay shared.</p><div class="ownership-lists"><div><h3>Parlor handles</h3><ul><li>Guest identity & room membership</li><li>Presence & host handoff</li><li>Match envelopes & participants</li></ul></div><div><h3>You make it yours</h3><ul><li>Game rules & hidden state</li><li>Turn order, timers & scores</li><li>Everything players see</li></ul></div></div><a class="button button-yellow" href="/docs/architecture/">Explore the architecture</a></div>
      <div class="code-panel"><div class="code-panel-heading"><span>convex/game.ts</span><span>Match lifecycle excerpt</span></div><Code code={matchCode} lang="ts" theme="github-dark" /><p><code>beginMatch</code> checks host authority and snapshots eligible players. <code>startYourGame</code> is your own game logic.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section container package-section" aria-labelledby="package-title"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="package-title">A small toolkit.<br />A full table.</h2><p>Five focused packages.<br />Use the pieces your game needs.</p></div><div class="package-list">{packages.map((pkg) => <a href="/docs/api/" class="package-row"><code>@parlor/{pkg.name}</code><strong>{pkg.text}</strong><span>{pkg.description}</span><span class="package-plus" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div><p class="release-note"><span class="release-tag">0.1.0</span> Source-distributed today, with an explicit setup guide. Pre-1.0 APIs may change. <a href="/docs/getting-started/">See installation & compatibility</a></p></section>

    <section id="in-the-wild" class="showcase-section container" aria-labelledby="showcase-title"><div class="poppycock-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="poppy-card card-back"></div><div class="poppy-card card-front"><span>The truth is<br />overrated.</span><strong>poppycock</strong><div class="poppy-bird"><i></i></div><small>Bluff. Vote. Reveal.</small></div><span class="poppy-sticker">3–12<br />players</span></div><div class="showcase-copy"><p class="section-kicker">Made with Parlor</p><h2 id="showcase-title">Meet Poppycock.</h2><p>A room full of friends. A very questionable answer. A bluffing game that turns everybody into a convincing liar.</p><p>Parlor powers its rooms, guests, presence, and matches. Poppycock brings the prompts, the points, and the poker faces.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="https://poppycock.mistystep.io">Play Poppycock <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/misty-step/poppycock">Explore the game’s source</a></div></div></section>

    <section class="section container agents-section" aria-labelledby="agents-title"><div><div class="agent-mark" aria-hidden="true">&lt; / &gt;</div><h2 id="agents-title">Your agent’s invited, too.</h2><p>Give your coding agent the same map you have. A portable skill, plain Markdown guides, and the boundaries that matter: server authority, private state, and who gets to play.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/agents/">Set up your agent</a></div><div class="agent-prompt"><span>A good place to start</span><pre data-copy><code>Read https://parlor.mistystep.io/skill.md
and the getting-started guide.

Help me build a phone-first party game
with Parlor, Convex, and React.

Keep game rules on the server. Use the
pinned source APIs. Verify the room flow
with separate player sessions.</code></pre><a href="/llms.txt">Browse the agent documentation index</a></div></section>

    <section class="closing-section"><div class="container"><div class="closing-pieces" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><h2>Good games start<br />with good company.</h2><p>Make something worth gathering around.</p><a class="button button-yellow" href="/docs/getting-started/">Build your first room</a><span class="closing-note">Open source. Yours to play with.</span></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
